<title>THAILAND: GOLF-BANGKOK CLASSIC, LEADING FINAL SCORES.</title>
<headline>GOLF-BANGKOK CLASSIC, LEADING FINAL SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading final round scores of</p>
<p>the $300,000 Bangkok Classic at the par-72 Thai Country Club on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>268 Tiger Woods (U.S.) 70 64 66 68</p>
<p>278 Mo Joong-kyung (South Korea) 70 70 70 70 68</p>
<p>279 Jim Rutledge (Canada) 69 75 72 63, Carlos Espinosa (Mexico)</p>
<p>68 68 74 69, Tse-peng Chang (Taiwan) 69 68 71 71</p>
<p>280 Chang-ting Yeh (Taiwan) 72 69 72 67, Brad Andrews</p>
<p>(Australia) 68 73 70 69, Mike Cunning (U.S.) 69 70 70 71</p>
<p>281 Arjun Atwal (India) 73 70 69 69, Frank Nobilo (New Zealand)</p>
<p>70 68 70 73</p>
<p>282 Steve Elkington (Australia) 71 71 71 69, Curtis Strange</p>
<p>(U.S) 68 74 71 69, Greg Hanrahan (U.S.) 70 66 70 76</p>
<p>283 Masayoshi Yamazoe (Japan) 72 74 70 67, Felix Casas</p>
<p>(Philippines) 71 75 70 67, M.Ramayah (Malaysia) 70 73 72</p>
<p>68, Paul Foley (Australia) 75 66 73 69, Danny Zarate</p>
<p>(Philippines) 72 72 68 71</p>
</text>
